    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0439" n="327" xml:id="pg327"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.51/306</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Scholle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-30T12:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 30, 1918, 12 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 29, 1 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d364-f1"/> I called personally on
                    Secretary of the Treasury on receipt of your April 20, 6 p.m., and urged him to
                    get me the information at once. He promised to attend to the matter himself.
                    Since then I have daily, through the Subsecretary of State, urged haste. Am
                    again to-day insisting on question being answered immediately.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Scholle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
